Slide 7 — CI Codebase: Git Branch

CI Codebase Configuration

Build Type

Git Branch

Branch Selection

The pipeline provides the option to specify the Git branch used for the deployment.

Two important possibilities:

<+trigger.branch>
        vs
Fixed Value

Manual Deployment

For the documented manual deployment process:

Select → Fixed Value

Then provide/select the branch that needs to be deployed.

Example

Build Type  : Git Branch
Branch Name : Fixed Value
Branch      : <intended branch>

Why?

Using a Fixed Value makes the deployment branch explicit during a manual pipeline execution.

