Slide 11 — Understanding Deployment Logs

What to Check in Deployment Logs

Deployment Execution

Review the deployment console/log output for:

* Deployment commands
* Target information
* Application/package deployment
* Command execution status
* Error messages
* Completion status

If Successful

Look for:

Deployment Started
       ↓
Commands Executed
       ↓
Deployment Completed
       ↓
Success

If Failed

Capture:

* Execution ID
* Failed stage
* Error message
* Relevant log section
* Deployment target

Then determine whether the issue is:

Code / Configuration / Target / Infrastructure / Application

